      <transcript>TAN-A</transcript>
      <definition>[tan + old dat.] To you (polite). Used after a title or name in addressing a letter, also in the opening words of a letter.</definition>
      <page>776</page>
      <examples>
        <example>
          <unicode>ᠡᠷᠺᠢᠮ ᠠᠪᠤᠭᠠᠢ ... ᠲᠠᠨᠨ᠎ᠠ</unicode>
          <transcript>erkim abuγai  . . - . </transcript>
          <definition>My dear Mr. . . .</definition>
        </example>
        <example>
          <unicode>ᠡᠷᠺᠢᠮ ᠨᠥᠺᠦᠷ ... ᠲᠠᠨᠨ᠎ᠠ</unicode>
          <transcript>erkim nøkyr  . . -- . </transcript>
          <definition>My dear friend . . .</definition>
        </example>
      </examples>
